<title>INDIA: Indian political parties' positions in parliament.</title>
<headline>Indian political parties' positions in parliament.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are political parties' current positions in India's lower house of parliament, the Lok Sabha, after the results of by-elections held in three constituencies on May 29.</p>
<p>The 545-seat Lok Sabha has two nominated members. Lok Sabha speaker P.A. Sangma is a member of the Congress party, but his affiliation is not taken into account in the party-wise break-up given below.</p>
<p>The National Conference, a regional party from the northern state of Jammu and Kashmir, has no Lok Sabha members but is represented in the upper house, the Rajya Sabha, and is part of Prime Minister Inder Kumar Gujral's 15-party United Front coalition.</p>
